Z||000000||fieroman_5000||10-19-2001||09:01 PM||||I have an 84 se auto. I started it up to take her out. after getting out of the garage I turned the key to accessory, (NOT 'OFF') to shut the garage door...when i was ready to start it up nothing happened. now I know that the battery is good, so I could'nt figure it out. So I tried turning the key to OFF and it would'nt turn??? Weird, I thought. I gave the key some pressure to get it out of the ignition. and now I can't turn it past lock.<P>What should I do??? Any help appreciated<P>Shane||||reg||5
Z||000001||Joe Torma||10-19-2001||09:52 PM||||Welcome to the forum!<P>Fot the heck of it, did you try turning the steering wheel back and forth while turning the key?<P>Otherwise, it sounds like the ignition rod and switch is jammed.  You'll probaby have to take the underside dash panel and probably the guage cluster off to see it.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||fieroman_5000||10-19-2001||10:09 PM||||I know it's not the steering lock.<BR>I think it's something like the ignition lock.||||reg||13
Z||000003||fieroman_5000||10-20-2001||07:27 PM||||Fixed!!!  I pulled the wheel and the lock plate and removed the lock cylinder and lubricated it VERY well. I guess there was some gunk in the locking mechanism.<BR>Shane <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
